      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The three checkout scripts the platform's site build runs for a repository that holds an IG and only mounts layers (`index.config.json`): `ig-site:ast` restores the AST from the IG's cache branch (`ig-cache.sh restore`) and judges it, refusing a stale, cannot-tell or absent one (a stale one is accepted for a preview with `SITE_ACCEPT_STALE_AST=1`); `ig-site:compose` derives the artefact index from the AST (binding any IG API sidecars a layer above left in `$SITE_WORK/ig-api/`), writes the thin artefact pages, stages the IG's `input/` and `sushi-config.yaml` (menu read at build time, palette from the webpage theme of the top layer the repository mounts, edit links from its origin) and composes it at the ROOT of the host site source; `ig-site:publisher-pages` serves the AST's resources (`ast-data/` and `<Type>-<id>.json`), the artefact index and the sidecars, refuses a page wearing the IG Publisher's chrome, repairs repeated element ids and stamps `folio-build.json`. Never runs the Publisher and never reads its output. Compose lists the pages it puts in the site in `FOLIO_SITE_UPSTREAM_PAGES`, so the site build reports the IG's own dead links rather than refusing the publish over them."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "ig-repo-site",
      "dcterms:source": "fhir-harness/tools/ig-repo-site/ig-repo-site.ts#ig-repo-site",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/fhir-harness/v0/ns#glossary/kg-tools/ig-site-data",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/fhir-harness/v0/ns#glossary/kg-tools"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Populate site.data.fhir for a just-the-docs IG render"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Write the IG Publisher's Jekyll variables (`site.data.fhir.ig.*`, `packageId`, `canonical`) for ONE implementation guide, from `sushi-config.yaml` or a published IG's `fhir-artifact-index`, so pages written for the Publisher render on just-the-docs unchanged. fhir-harness declares `site.data` as a pass-through Liquid prefix; this is what Jekyll then reads (bean `bamf`)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "ig-site-data",
      "dcterms:source": "fhir-harness/tools/ig-site-data/ig-site-data.ts#ig-site-data",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/fhir-harness/v0/ns#glossary/kg-tools/ingest-ig-menu",
